# PART 2 — TARGET ARCHITECTURE

Build a modular architecture with a unified coordinator and specialized download engines.

```text
Novay Download Center
│
├── Batch Download Coordinator
│   ├── Episode Selection
│   ├── Season Downloads
│   ├── Multi-Season Downloads
│   └── Batch Progress Aggregation
│
├── Global Queue Scheduler
│   ├── Queue Management
│   ├── Priority Management
│   ├── Concurrency Control
│   └── Network Constraints
│
├── Download Engine Router
│   ├── Direct HTTP / MP4 Engine
│   │   └── Downpour candidate / compatible adapter
│   │
│   └── Adaptive Media Engine
│       └── AndroidX Media3
│           ├── HLS / M3U8
│           └── DASH / MPD
│
├── Persistence Layer
│   ├── Room Metadata
│   ├── Batch Relationships
│   ├── Queue Ordering
│   └── Engine State Reconciliation
│
├── Background Execution
│   ├── Appropriate Android Service or Job
│   ├── WorkManager where suitable
│   └── Notifications
│
├── Offline Playback Integration
│
└── Download Center UI
    ├── Active
    ├── Queue
    ├── Completed
    ├── Failed
    └── Batches
```

### Architecture rules

- Use one unified download model for the UI.
- Keep each engine responsible for its own transfer state.
- The coordinator must translate engine-specific states into Novay's unified state model.
- Avoid maintaining two competing sources of truth for progress.
- Room should store Novay metadata, batch relationships, priorities, ordering and engine identifiers.
- Media3 must retain ownership of its download index.
- If Downpour is adopted, respect its own persistence and state management.
- Reconcile engine state with Novay metadata after process death or application restart.
- Do not duplicate large media files unnecessarily.

Create clean interfaces and separate responsibilities.

Suggested abstraction:

```kotlin
interface DownloadEngine {
    suspend fun enqueue(request: DownloadRequest): String
    suspend fun pause(id: String)
    suspend fun resume(id: String)
    suspend fun cancel(id: String)
    suspend fun retry(id: String)
    suspend fun remove(id: String)
    suspend fun deleteOfflineData(id: String)

    fun observe(id: String): Flow<DownloadItem>
    fun observeAll(): Flow<List<DownloadItem>>
}
```

Adapt the interface to the actual capabilities of each engine. Do not pretend an engine supports an operation that it cannot safely perform.

