# PART 3 — DOWNLOAD FORMATS AND ENGINES

Support the following formats:

| Format | Engine |
|---|---|
| Direct MP4 | HTTP engine |
| Direct HTTP/HTTPS | HTTP engine |
| HLS / M3U8 | AndroidX Media3 |
| DASH / MPD | AndroidX Media3 |

## A. Direct HTTP / MP4

Evaluate Downpour first:

https://github.com/AlirezaJavan/Downpour

It is a Kotlin download library using Coroutines, Flow, Room and OkHttp.

Evaluate its:

- Persistent queue.
- Pause and resume support.
- Retry handling.
- Network handling.
- Progress reporting.
- Background execution.
- Integrity validation.
- Compatibility with Novay's existing architecture.

Do not blindly add it as a dependency. Verify its current release, API, manifest requirements, minSdk, transitive dependencies and compatibility first.

If it is unsuitable, implement a dedicated adapter or another appropriately maintained solution.

### HTTP resume requirements

Use HTTP Range requests when supported.

Validate:

- `Accept-Ranges`.
- `206 Partial Content`.
- `Content-Range`.
- `ETag`.
- `Last-Modified`.

Never append data to an existing partial file if the server returns a full response or the remote resource has changed.

Resume must only be advertised when the server supports safe resumption.

Support:

- Streaming writes.
- Temporary files.
- Safe completion and publication.
- Filename collision handling.
- Retry with bounded exponential backoff.
- Integrity checks when a checksum is available.

Never load an entire video into memory.

## B. HLS / M3U8 and DASH / MPD

Use AndroidX Media3's official download implementation.

Primary documentation:

https://developer.android.com/media/media3/exoplayer/downloading-media

Use the appropriate Media3 components:

- `DownloadService`
- `DownloadManager`
- `DownloadIndex`
- `DownloadRequest`
- `DownloadHelper`
- `SimpleCache`
- `CacheDataSource.Factory`

Requirements:

- Download HLS and DASH as adaptive media.
- Support offline track selection where possible.
- Support video, audio and subtitle tracks where available.
- Persist download state through Media3.
- Integrate Media3's cache with Novay's existing player.
- Support offline playback without a network connection.
- Use the same appropriate cache for downloaded playback.
- Respect Media3's supported removal and cache APIs.

Do not treat HLS/DASH segments as ordinary MP4 files.

Do not manually manipulate Media3's internal cache files.

Keep all Media3 dependencies aligned with the version already used by Novay.

