# PART 8 — BACKGROUND EXECUTION AND NOTIFICATIONS

Use Android's current recommended background execution APIs.

References:

https://developer.android.com/develop/background-work/background-tasks/uidt

https://developer.android.com/develop/background-work/background-tasks/data-transfer-options

https://developer.android.com/develop/background-work/background-tasks/persistent/how-to/long-running

Evaluate the appropriate solution for each transfer type and Android version.

Consider:

- User-Initiated Data Transfer (UIDT) jobs on eligible Android 14+ devices.
- Foreground services when appropriate and permitted.
- WorkManager for suitable deferrable or recoverable work.
- Media3's DownloadService for adaptive downloads.

Important:

- Do not assume WorkManager guarantees uninterrupted long downloads.
- Do not assume foreground services can run indefinitely.
- Respect Android 15+ foreground-service time limits.
- Handle `Service.onTimeout()` where applicable.
- Respect notification permissions.
- Handle process death, reboot, force-stop and network changes.
- Do not use unsupported background execution workarounds.

### Notifications

Provide useful notifications showing:

- Current episode or batch.
- Download progress.
- Downloaded size.
- Speed when available.
- Completion or failure.
- Pause/resume actions where supported.

Batch notifications should summarize the batch without losing per-episode information in the Download Center.

